.TH NAME
g2 \- Gentoo overlay and repository maintenance utilities


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBg2\fP [\fICOMMAND\fP] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fP] [\fIFLAGS\fP] [\fIARGS...\fP]


.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBg2\fP is a collection of command-line utilities for creating, managing, and working with Gentoo overlay repositories. It provides tools for manipulating \fBManifest\fR files, updating \fBmetadata.xml\fR, interacting with ebuilds, linting repositories, and generating static HTML sites representing overlays.

.PP
The command set supports local overlay maintenance as well as comprehensive tools to index and serve search data.


.SH COMMANDS
.SH \fBmanifest\fR
Commands relating to \fBManifest\fP files.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBupsert-from-url\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Downloads a file from \fI\fP, calculates required checksums, and updates or inserts the entry into the \fBManifest\fR file.
Flags: \fB-blake2b\fR, \fB-blake2s\fR, \fB-md5\fR, \fB-rmd160\fR, \fB-sha1\fR, \fB-sha256\fR, \fB-sha3_256\fR, \fB-sha3_512\fR, \fB-sha512\fR (default: \fBblake2b\fR and \fBsha512\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBverify\fP [\fI--fix\fP] [\fI--clean\fP] \fI\fP
Verifies the \fBManifest\fR entries against the ebuild URIs. If \fB--fix\fR is passed, missing entries will be downloaded and upserted. If \fB--clean\fR is passed, unused entries will be removed.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBclean\fP \fI\fP
Removes unused entries from the \fBManifest\fR file.

.SH \fBmetadata\fR
Commands relating to modifying \fBmetadata.xml\fP files.

.PP
Usage: \fBg2 metadata [flags] [location]\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-l, -longdescription\fP \fI\fP
Set the long description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-m, -maintainer-add\fP \fI\fP
Add or update a maintainer.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-maintainer-remove\fP \fI\fP
Remove a maintainer.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-u, -upstream-add\fP \fI
\[la]type:id\[ra]\fP
Add an upstream remote ID (e.g., \fBgithub:gentoo/gentoo\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-upstream-remove\fP \fI
\[la]type:id\[ra]\fP
Remove an upstream remote ID.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-use, -use-add\fP \fI
\[la]name:description\[ra]\fP
Add or update a USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-use-remove\fP \fI\fP
Remove a USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-force\fP
Force overwrite if type mismatches or other errors occur.

.SS \fBmetadata discover\fR
Discover flags and metadata.

.SH \fBebuild\fR
Commands for manipulating and inspecting \fB\&.ebuild\fP files.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinit\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Initializes a new ebuild from the specified template.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtemplates\fP
Manages ebuild templates.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsh-parse-to-json\fP \fI\fP
Parses an ebuild using the shell parser and outputs JSON.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBas-json\fP \fI\fP
Parses an ebuild natively into JSON format.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBexplain\fP \fI\fP
Output a human-readable summary of an ebuild.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBquery\fP \fI\fP \fB--key\fR \fI\fP [\fB--format\fR \fIlines\fP]
Queries specific fields from a parsed ebuild output, rather than dumping the whole JSON.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcheck-exists\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Determine if any revision of a given version exists, returning exit code 0 if found and 1 if not.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnext-revision\fP [\fI--inspect \fP] \fI\fP \fI\fP
Generate the next revision name. If \fB--inspect\fR is provided and the contents match the current highest revision, it outputs the current revision and exits 1. Otherwise, it outputs the bumped revision and exits 0.

.SH \fBoverlay\fR
Commands for managing a single overlay.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBebuild move\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Record a package move in \fBprofiles/updates\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBebuild slotmove\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Record a slot move in \fBprofiles/updates\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBebuild install\fP [\fI--category \fP] \fI\fP [\fIoverlay_path\fP] [\fI-- files...\fP]
Installs an ebuild into the overlay, optionally providing files for the \fBfiles/\fR directory. Automatically triggers manifest, cache, use desc, and pkg_desc_index generation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsite generate\fP [\fI--out \fP] [\fI--clear\fP] [\fIlocation\fP]
Generates a static HTML site for the overlay.
Flags: \fB-out\fR (default: \fBsite_out\fR), \fB-clear\fR, \fB-fast-git-modtime\fR, \fB-recent-duration\fR\&.
Writes RSS 2.0 and Atom feeds for available news to \fBnews/index.rss\fR and \fBnews/index.atom\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlicense list\fP
Lists all configured licenses.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlicense show\fP \fI\fP
Shows the contents of a license.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlicense add\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Adds a new license from a file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlicense remove\fP \fI\fP
Removes a license.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlicense alias\fP [\fIlist|add|remove\fP]
Manages license aliases (groups).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinfo-vars\fP [\fIlist|add|remove\fP]
Manages info variables.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinfo-pkgs\fP [\fIlist|add|remove\fP]
Manages info packages.

.SH \fBoverlays\fR
Commands for working across multiple overlays.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsite generate\fP [\fI--out \fP] [\fI--clear\fP] \fI\fP
Generates an aggregated static HTML site for multiple remote repositories described in a \fBrepositories.xml\fR file.
Writes combined RSS 2.0 and Atom news feeds below \fBnews/\fR and repository news feeds below \fBrepos/<repository>/news/\fR\&.

.SH \fBsite\fR
Commands relating to generated static sites.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBserve\fP [\fI--port \fP] [\fIpath_to_overlay\fP]
Serves the generated static site locally for previewing. Defaults to port 8080.

.SH \fBlint\fR
Lints the repository for QA issues and consistency errors.

.PP
Usage: \fBg2 lint [location]\fR

.PP
Checks for:
- Missing \fBmd5-cache\fR files
- \fBIUSE\fR variables missing from \fBmetadata.xml\fR
- Unsupported \fBlayout.conf\fR properties
- Orphaned \fBManifest\fR entries
- Missing keywords
- And more.

.SH \fBuse\fR
Commands for working with \fBUSE flags\fP, \fBuse.desc\fP, and \fBuse.local.desc\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdiscover\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Discovers USE flags from ebuilds to regenerate \fBuse.desc\fR, \fBuse.local.desc\fR, and \fBmetadata.xml\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdesc-add\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Adds a global USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdesc-remove\fP \fI\fP
Removes a global USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdesc-edit\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Edits a global USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdesc-list\fP
Lists global USE flag descriptions.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlocal-desc-add\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Adds a local USE flag description for a specific package.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlocal-desc-remove\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Removes a local USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlocal-desc-edit\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP \fI\fP
Edits a local USE flag description.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlocal-desc-list\fP
Lists all local USE flag descriptions.

.SH \fBcache\fR
Commands for managing \fBmd5-dict\fP cache files.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgenerate\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Generates \fBmd5-dict\fR cache for ebuilds.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBverify\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Verifies the cache matches the ebuilds.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBclean\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Cleans unused cache entries.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlist-methods\fP
Lists available caching methods.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBset-method\fP \fI\fP
Sets the active cache method in \fBlayout.conf\fR\&.

.SH \fBpkg-desc-index\fR
Commands for maintaining the package description index.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgenerate\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Generates a \fBpkg_desc_index\fR file from the repository.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBverify\fP [\fIlocation\fP]
Verifies the existing \fBpkg_desc_index\fR matches the repository.

.SH \fBpackage\fR
Commands relating to package search and indexing.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsearch\fP [\fI--path \fP] \fI\fP
Searches the index for packages matching the query. Advanced queries support boolean logic (AND, OR, NOT), grouping, and Gentoo version ordering (e.g., \fBversion:>1.2.3\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBindex-overlay\fP
Indexes a single overlay for search.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBindex-repositories\fP
Indexes multiple repositories from an XML file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBindex\fP
Indexes local repositories.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBupdate\fP
Updates the local index from a remote ZIP file.

.SH \fBlayout-conf\fR
Tools to manipulate \fBmetadata/layout.conf\fR values.

.PP
Usage: \fBg2 layout-conf list\fR
Usage: \fBg2 layout-conf <element> [get|set|unset]\fR


.SH EXAMPLES
Download an archive, calculate SHA256 in addition to the defaults, and update the Manifest in the current directory:
    $ g2 manifest -sha256=true upsert-from-url https://example.com/software-1.0.tar.gz software-1.0.tar.gz .

.PP
Add a maintainer to \fBmetadata.xml\fR:
    $ g2 metadata -maintainer-add "dev@example.com:Developer Name:person" .

.PP
Install a package into a specific category, including extra files:
    $ g2 overlay ebuild install -category sys-apps my-app-1.0.ebuild . -- app.conf app.service

.PP
Generate a static HTML site for the overlay:
    $ g2 overlay site generate -out my_site_dir .

.PP
Serve the generated static site locally:
    $ g2 site serve -port 8080 .

.PP
Discover and populate USE flags automatically:
    $ g2 use discover .

.PP
Generate the ebuild cache for the current overlay:
    $ g2 cache generate .


.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
